      "writtenOn": "2025-06-25T21:49:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`try_verify_in_tasklet` is actually a mis-nomer now, since it doesn\u0027t actually use tasklets anymore.  It does use softirq context, either through inline work or the \"bottom-half workqueue\", which achieves a similar effect.\n\nThe point is, I\u0027d prefer something like:\n\n```\n// Enable processing of short requests in softirq context (if supported)\ntarget.TryVerifyInTasklet();\n```\n\nThat way the mention of \"tasklet\" would be more limited to just the name of the option.",
